<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">German Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kaiserreich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The German Empire was the unified German state proclaimed in 1871 under Prussian leadership after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-prussian-war">Franco-Prussian War</a>. It became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s leading industrial power, acquired colonies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and the Pacific and built a large navy, but it was defeated in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> and collapsed in 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/german-empire.jpg" alt="German Empire" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Adolf Soetbeer, Otto von Bismarck Vector: B1mbo, Madden · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Germany_(1867%E2%80%931918).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…Conrad and Frederick at first held the inheritance together and then divided it, probably by about 1218: Conrad took the burgraviate of Nuremberg and founded the Franconian line, which later ruled Brandenburg, Prussia and the <b>German Empire</b>, while Frederick kept the ancestral Swabian lands as Count of Zollern.</blockquote><a href="/empire/county-of-hohenzollern">County of Hohenzollern · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Hamburg joined the North German Confederation in 1867 and the <b>German Empire</b> in 1871 as a federal state, entering the customs union in 1888 on condition of keeping a free port.</blockquote><a href="/empire/free-and-hanseatic-city-of-hamburg">Free and Hanseatic City of Hamburg · Into the Present</a></li><li><blockquote>It joined the North German Confederation in 1867 and the <b>German Empire</b> in 1871 as a federal state with its own Senate, entering the German customs union only in 1888, when it was granted a free port.</blockquote><a href="/empire/free-hanseatic-city-of-bremen">Free Hanseatic City of Bremen · Into the Present</a></li><li><blockquote>Its federal structure, with sovereign states represented by government envoys, influenced the Bundesrat of the North German Confederation and the <b>German Empire</b>, an element that survives in the Bundesrat of the Federal Republic of Germany.</blockquote><a href="/empire/german-confederation">German Confederation · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Within the <b>German Empire</b> the grand duchy kept its own government and parliament.</blockquote><a href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-hesse">Grand Duchy of Hesse · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>Under the treaty by which Bavaria entered the <b>German Empire</b>, its army remained under the king's command in peacetime and passed to the emperor only in war.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-bavaria">Kingdom of Bavaria · Military</a></li></ul></section>
